/-!
# Two movers, frozen readings 124: a common clear instant in the first wide piece for ALL movers beyond the least frozen reading (GENERATED by `s2_gen_lean_clean_v1.py`)

Written 2026-10-23.  New file.  First wide piece `[1/8, 7/32]` (the first lonely piece of the frozen set).  For ALL real `d1, d2 > 1`
(no grid, no threshold) the two movers have a common clear instant in the piece (`exists_common_clear_124`), hence the landing mechanism of
`land2C124` (`land2_all_124`).  Method: a finite box cover of `{d1 ≤ d2}` (`10` columns in `d1`, `17` boxes), each box certified by a lemma of
`S2CleanLemmas` (rule R1 `r1_rect`, or a point witness `wit_pt`) with explicit numerals; `d1 > 11` (D0) by `big_both` [PROVISIONAL: counting tool].
Grades: [L]; the existence statement is discharged by a finite box cover [PROVISIONAL: covering].  Box kinds: {'P': 6, 'R1a': 10, 'R1b': 1}.
Not proved here: the cascade's path inside the piece; movers at or below `1`.
